svg-editor 0.1 — type 'help' for commands
svg> svg> svg> init [w] [h] — create canvas (default 800x600)
canvas [w h] — inspect or resize canvas
create <type> <id> [params...] [in <containerId>] — create a shape
tree [id] — show scene or subtree
show <id> — show parent and attributes
move <id> <dx> <dy> — translate a shape or group
scale <id> <factor> — scale all geometry by a positive factor
set <id> <attr> <value> — set a whitelisted attribute
delete <id> — delete a shape and its descendants
group <newGid> <id1> <id2>... — group existing shapes in document order
ungroup <gid> — promote a nested group's children
addto <gid> <id> — move an existing shape into a container
front <id> — move to the last sibling slot (painted in front)
back <id> — move to the first sibling slot
read <file.svg> — load SVG as the current document
save [file.svg] — save SVG (path required without a read source)
undo — undo the last edit
redo — redo the last undone edit
help — show command syntax
create rect <id> <x> <y> <w> <h> [fill] — rectangle
create circle <id> <cx> <cy> <r> [fill] — circle
create ellipse <id> <cx> <cy> <rx> <ry> [fill] — ellipse
create line <id> <x1> <y1> <x2> <y2> [stroke] — line
create text <id> <x> <y> "content" — text
create g <id> — empty group; all creates accept in <containerId>
EOF — exit (Ctrl+Z then Enter on Windows; Ctrl+D on Unix).
svg> canvas 800x600 created
svg> svg (800x600)
svg> svg> rect#r1 created
svg> svg> svg> svg> svg> text#t1 created
svg> text#t1 updated: text=""
